- lib/webcmds.js: one pass over web\**\*.js and the pages' inline scripts
  (JSON\ data skipped): command -> where the web sends it, and which pages
  load that script
- CodeLens above `== "x.y"` / `case "x.y":` in C++: "網頁送出 io.btnPanelClick：
  ht9045_io_do.js:194（HW.IoSetView.html）", click -> the web line
  (66 such lines in wb_serve.cpp)
- JS comments are skipped when looking for sends (a doc-comment example in
  ht9045_io_do.js:9 used to count); the panel's "送出命令" row too
- the index is rebuilt (debounced) when a web .js/.html changes, never for
  JSON\ which the running system may rewrite

Tests: lib 58 / probe 2 pages / fake vscode 35 / real VS Code 40 incl.
8-page sweep -- all pass, 12 opened files byte-identical (MD5).

